From: Vivek Kumar Verma <vivekverma@arista.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:31:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6.12 1/1] net: ftgmac100: hard-reset MAC only for Marvell 88E151x

Upstream-Status: Pending

On AST2700 + Marvell 88E151x over SGMII, an "ifconfig down/up" (or a
partner-side link flap) intermittently leaves the MAC receive path wedged:
the link comes back up and reports resolved, TX works, but RX stays frozen
(no DHCP, no ping). The MDIO/serdes registers look identical to a healthy
link in this state, so the wedge is below the register layer.

The only reliable recovery is "modprobe -r ftgmac100 / modprobe ftgmac100",
which re-runs probe and performs a full reset_control cycle of the MAC IP
block. The ndo_open/ftgmac100_reset() path only issues the soft MACCR reset,
which does not clear the wedged RX path.

ftgmac100_reset_and_config_mac() already hard-resets RMII. For SGMII, run
the reset_control cycle only when the Clause 22 PHY ID matches
MARVELL_PHY_ID_88E1510 under MARVELL_PHY_ID_MASK. This limits the
workaround to the Marvell 88E151x family and avoids breaking Broadcom
SGMII links.

Signed-off-by: Vivek Kumar Verma <vivekverma@arista.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c
index 035fa1c2b1fb..24fff91b1db4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_mdio.h>
 #include <linux/phy.h>
+#include <linux/marvell_phy.h>
 #include <linux/phy/phy.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
@@ -156,9 +157,18 @@ static int ftgmac100_reset_and_config_mac(struct ftgmac100 *priv)
 static int ftgmac100_reset_and_config_mac(struct ftgmac100 *priv)
 {
+	struct phy_device *phydev = priv->netdev->phydev;
 	u32 maccr = 0;
 
-	/* RMII needs SCU reset to clear status */
-	if (priv->netdev->phydev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RMII) {
+	/*
+	 * RMII needs SCU reset to clear status. AST2700 SGMII links with
+	 * Marvell 88E151x can wedge MAC RX after a down/up or link flap.
+	 * Limit this hard reset to that PHY family; Broadcom links fail
+	 * when subjected to it.
+	 */
+	if (phydev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RMII ||
+	    (phydev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII &&
+	     phy_id_compare(phydev->phy_id, MARVELL_PHY_ID_88E1510,
+			    MARVELL_PHY_ID_MASK))) {
 		int err;
 
 		err = reset_control_assert(priv->rst);
